<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκηθής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unhurt, unscathed,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἂψ εἰς ἡμέας ἔλθοι ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.212
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἱκόμην ἐς πατρίδα γαῖαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.79
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				99.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				3.1.69
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκηθέες</span> (trisyll.) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καὶ ἄνουσοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.255
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσκεθέες</span>
			); <i>sound, healthy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				4.952.109
			</span></i> (Epid.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινὰ πέμπειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sol.
					19.4
				</span></i>
			; <i>unblemished,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				5(2).3.5
			</span></i> (Tegea, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>); 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαθής, θεός</span>
			 Timo <i><span class="en">
				60
			</span></i>, etc.; later of things, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. νόστος</span>
			<i>safe</i> return, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.690
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. μέλι</span>
			<i>pure, virgin</i> honey, <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
				16.2
			</span></i>. (Perh. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> priv., and
			the root of <i>scathe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Germ.
			</span></i>
			<i>schaden</i> 'hurt'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
